WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.140
Hi, Tealy here.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.400
Vocabulary questions aren't testing whether you memorized

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.520
a dictionary. They're testing whether you can read.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.260
The researcher advanced a hypothesis.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.640
What does advanced mean here?

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.220
Your brain says:

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.740
moved forward. Like somebody walking.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.060
But hypotheses don't walk.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.360
So cover the choices,

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.700
and cover the word.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.780
The researcher, blank,

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.400
a hypothesis. What simple word would you put there?

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.040
Suggested. Proposed. Now you have a meaning,

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.720
before you even see the options.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.400
Then uncover the choices,

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.800
and compare meanings.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.820
Moved forward? No.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.780
Proposed? That's your word.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.500
Improved? No.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.440
A word means what the author is using it to mean,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.580
in this sentence.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.600
The car advanced.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.720
It moved forward.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.760
The researcher advanced a hypothesis.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:01.280
She proposed it.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.840
Same word, different job.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.840
Your turn. The critic's review was sharp.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.460
Does sharp mean pointed,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.360
like a knife,

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.440
or harsh? Go.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.820
Harsh! A review can't cut paper.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.300
A familiar dictionary meaning can be wrong in this sentence.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.280
So check the tone.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:27.900
Is the writer being kind,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:28.800
or harsh?

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.780
And check the grammar too.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.340
The researcher proposal a hypothesis?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.100
Nope. Proposed fits.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.300
Then reread the sentence with your choice in it.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.480
If it still makes sense,

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:41.580
you've got it.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.920
Now hit Try this skill!
